## Pull Request: Fix race condition in DataProcessor

**Changes:**
- Added a new synchronized block to the `processData` method to prevent concurrent writes.
- Updated unit tests to cover the new synchronization logic.
- Refactored `DataProcessorHelper` to remove deprecated methods.

**Diff summary:**
```diff
+    public void processData(Data input) {
+        synchronized(this) {
+            // New synchronization to avoid race conditions
+            if (input == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException("input cannot be null");
+            // Process the data
+            this.state = computeState(input);
+        }
+    }
-
-    // Deprecated method removed
-    public void oldProcess(Data input) {
-        // old implementation
-    }
+
+    // Updated unit test to assert thread safety
+    @Test
+    public void testProcessDataThreadSafety() throws InterruptedException {
+        DataProcessor processor = new DataProcessor();
+        Runnable task = () -> processor.processData(new Data("test"));
+        Thread t1 = new Thread(task);
+        Thread t2 = new Thread(task);
+        t1.start();
+        t2.start();
+        t1.join();
+        t2.join();
+        assertNotNull(processor.getState());
+    }
```

