## Pull Request: Refactor authentication flow

This PR refactors the login process to use async/await instead of callbacks and introduces a new `AuthService` class. The changes include:
- Replacing `loginUser(callback)` calls with `await authService.login(username, password)` in `src/components/LoginForm.vue`.
- Adding `src/services/AuthService.js` which contains `login`, `logout`, and `refreshToken` methods.
- Updating unit tests in `tests/unit/AuthService.spec.js` to cover the new async behavior.
- Modifying the CI pipeline to run ESLint with the `no-undef` rule stricter.

### Diff Summary
```diff
+ src/services/AuthService.js
@@
- // Old callback based login
- export function loginUser(username, password, cb) {
-   api.post('/login', { username, password })
-     .then(res => cb(null, res.data))
-     .catch(err => cb(err));
- }
+ // New async/await based login
+ export default class AuthService {
+   async login(username, password) {
+     const response = await api.post('/login', { username, password });
+     return response.data;
+   }
+   // ... other methods
+ }
```

